   "title": {
    "zh": "给每个点一个数",
    "en": "A Number for Every Point"
   },
   "why": {
    "zh": "从撒了沙的振动金属板讲起：沙聚成一条线，把板分成两半。再看五个朋友沿一条长凳站开，交情越深的橡皮筋越粗、拉得越紧；他们停下的位置就是 Fiedler 向量，剪刀逐个缝隙试一刀。还有镜像翻号、彼此不认识的两群人，以及 15 而不是 16。",
    "en": "It opens with sand on a bowed metal plate, gathering on one line that splits it in two. Then five friends spread along a bench, tied by rubber bands that pull harder the closer they are; where they settle is the Fiedler vector, and scissors try every gap. Plus a mirror flip, two groups who never met, and 15, not 16."
   },
