     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 4.6,
       "text": "Sprinkle fine sand on a metal plate,",
       "sceneId": "p-plate"
      },
      {
       "start": 4.6,
       "end": 9.2,
       "text": "and draw a violin bow along its edge.",
       "sceneId": "p-plate"
      },
      {
       "start": 10.75,
       "end": 16.35,
       "text": "The sand gathers on one line: the vibration splits the plate in two.",
       "sceneId": "p-plate2"
      },
      {
       "start": 17.41,
       "end": 21.766,
       "text": "Five friends on a bench, tied by rubber bands.",
       "sceneId": "p-rule"
      },
      {
       "start": 21.766,
       "end": 26.566,
       "text": "Total pull: thickness times distance squared, added up.",
       "sceneId": "p-rule"
      },
      {
       "start": 26.566,
       "end": 31.166,
       "text": "No huddling on one spot: spread out, with the least pull.",
       "sceneId": "p-rule"
      },
      {
       "start": 37.0,
       "end": 41.2,
       "text": "Let go, and the bands pull everyone into place.",
       "sceneId": "p-settle"
      },
      {
       "start": 41.2,
       "end": 44.4,
       "text": "Close friends are pulled together.",
       "sceneId": "p-settle"
      },
      {
       "start": 44.4,
       "end": 50.978,
       "text": "Eva, Dev left; Ben, Ada right; Cai between.",
       "sceneId": "p-settle"
      },
      {
       "start": 51.18,
       "end": 54.18,
       "text": "Read off each person's position.",
       "sceneId": "p-numbers"
      },
      {
       "start": 54.18,
       "end": 58.313,
       "text": "That list of numbers is the Fiedler vector.",
       "sceneId": "p-numbers"
      },
      {
       "start": 58.313,
       "end": 61.713,
       "text": "Close friends get close numbers.",
       "sceneId": "p-numbers"
      },
      {
       "start": 63.15,
       "end": 67.506,
       "text": "Now try a cut at every gap along the bench.",
       "sceneId": "p-scissors"
      },
      {
       "start": 67.506,
       "end": 71.417,
       "text": "Friendship split: 6, 3, 5, 6.",
       "sceneId": "p-scissors"
      },
      {
       "start": 71.417,
       "end": 75.994,
       "text": "Two or three a side: take 3, not the middle.",
       "sceneId": "p-scissors"
      },
      {
       "start": 80.16,
       "end": 83.56,
       "text": "Multiply every number by minus one —",
       "sceneId": "p-mirror"
      },
      {
       "start": 83.56,
       "end": 86.56,
       "text": "the whole line mirrors over.",
       "sceneId": "p-mirror"
      },
      {
       "start": 89.0,
       "end": 93.133,
       "text": "Still the same cut, with left and right renamed.",
       "sceneId": "p-same"
      },
      {
       "start": 93.133,
       "end": 96.133,
       "text": "A sign flip is not a new answer.",
       "sceneId": "p-same"
      },
      {
       "start": 102.5,
       "end": 106.411,
       "text": "What if they are two groups who never met?",
       "sceneId": "p-apart"
      },
      {
       "start": 106.411,
       "end": 110.211,
       "text": "Everyone in a group lands on the same number.",
       "sceneId": "p-apart"
      },
      {
       "start": 110.211,
       "end": 116.211,
       "text": "Then λ₂ = 0: the numbers only say who connects. Check connectivity first.",
       "sceneId": "p-apart"
      },
      {
       "start": 119.27,
       "end": 122.959,
       "text": "How many ways to split five people in two?",
       "sceneId": "p-count"
      },
      {
       "start": 122.959,
       "end": 127.759,
       "text": "Left or right each: 32, minus all-left and all-right.",
       "sceneId": "p-count"
      },
      {
       "start": 127.759,
       "end": 132.337,
       "text": "Swapping sides is the same: 15, not 16.",
       "sceneId": "p-count"
      },
      {
       "start": 134.16,
       "end": 139.56,
       "text": "On a chip, this cut is often where partitioning starts.",
       "sceneId": "p-chip"
      },
      {
       "start": 141.5,
       "end": 147.5,
       "text": "One number each, from the whole graph.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 147.5,
       "end": 153.5,
       "text": "Along the line, try every gap.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 153.5,
       "end": 160.5,
       "text": "What you get is a good candidate, not a guarantee.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 160.5,
       "end": 168.5,
       "text": "After the cut, what about swapping people across? See the next module.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 170.6,
       "end": 176.6,
       "text": "In the lab below, change a weight and watch the line move.",
       "sceneId": "p-end"
      }
     ],
