     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 7.533,
       "text": "Spectral bisection splits a graph into two groups.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 7.533,
       "end": 9.8,
       "text": "Both groups non-empty.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 9.8,
       "end": 17.267,
       "text": "And a declared balance window, here 2 to 3 a side; inside it, make the cut small.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 17.267,
       "end": 21.4,
       "text": "Five nodes have 15 non-empty bipartitions.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 21.8,
       "end": 26.6,
       "text": "Step one: build the Laplacian L = D − A.",
       "sceneId": "k02-laplacian"
      },
      {
       "start": 26.6,
       "end": 32.289,
       "text": "Row A: degree 5 + 1 = 6, −5 to B, −1 to C.",
       "sceneId": "k02-laplacian"
      },
      {
       "start": 32.289,
       "end": 34.689,
       "text": "Every row sums to 0.",
       "sceneId": "k02-laplacian"
      },
      {
       "start": 35.089,
       "end": 42.089,
       "text": "Why L? Look at the quadratic form: each edge adds w times the squared difference of its ends.",
       "sceneId": "k03-quad"
      },
      {
       "start": 42.089,
       "end": 46.689,
       "text": "The heavier the edge, the closer its two numbers must be.",
       "sceneId": "k03-quad"
      },
      {
       "start": 46.689,
       "end": 52.6,
       "text": "Among unit vectors orthogonal to all-ones, the minimum is λ₂.",
       "sceneId": "k03-quad"
      },
      {
       "start": 52.6,
       "end": 57.178,
       "text": "The vector that attains it is the Fiedler vector.",
       "sceneId": "k03-quad"
      },
      {
       "start": 57.578,
       "end": 63.267,
       "text": "G01's Fiedler vector gives each node a number.",
       "sceneId": "k04-fiedler"
      },
      {
       "start": 63.267,
       "end": 66.956,
       "text": "The order: E, D, C, B, A.",
       "sceneId": "k04-fiedler"
      },
      {
       "start": 66.956,
       "end": 72.644,
       "text": "Tightly linked nodes sit together; C, linked to both sides, sits between.",
       "sceneId": "k04-fiedler"
      },
      {
       "start": 73.044,
       "end": 77.778,
       "text": "Along the order, try a cut between each pair of neighbours.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sweep"
      },
      {
       "start": 77.778,
       "end": 81.689,
       "text": "The cuts are 6, 3, 5, 6.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sweep"
      },
      {
       "start": 81.689,
       "end": 88.489,
       "text": "Only k = 2 and 3 are in the window: choose k = 2 with cut 3, not the middle.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sweep"
      },
      {
       "start": 88.889,
       "end": 94.133,
       "text": "Two warnings. First, the sign: −x is an eigenvector too.",
       "sceneId": "k06-warn"
      },
      {
       "start": 94.133,
       "end": 98.267,
       "text": "The order reverses; the same cut just swaps sides.",
       "sceneId": "k06-warn"
      },
      {
       "start": 98.267,
       "end": 104.8,
       "text": "Second, when the graph is disconnected λ₂ = 0, and the order only reflects components.",
       "sceneId": "k06-warn"
      },
      {
       "start": 105.2,
       "end": 107.333,
       "text": "Four things to keep.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 107.333,
       "end": 110.6,
       "text": "Declare non-empty sides and a window;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 110.6,
       "end": 115.178,
       "text": "build L, sort by Fiedler, sweep;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 115.178,
       "end": 120.711,
       "text": "Sign flips change nothing; check connectivity. Try it in the lab below.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      }
     ],
